"does this first\" suggests normalizing the sku first. In `add`, normalize is called first, then checkQuantity. Same for `reserve`. `remove`: normalize then checkQuantity. `release`: currently checkQuantity first, then uses sku without normalization. After the fix, should normalize come first to match \"does this first\"? The rule says \"all methods that accept a SKU do this first\" — \"first\" probably means before using the SKU. To be safe and consistent, put normalizeSku first in release as well.\n\nAlso for `release` on an unknown sku: since sku normalization may throw TypeError, if the sku isn't a string, it throws TypeError. No problem.\n\nLet me also check whether `#entry` is used anywhere else... no problem.\n\nAny other subtle bugs? R2 \"quantity must be a positive integer, otherwise the method throws a RangeError. Applies to add, remove, reserve, release.\" checkQuantity handles them all.\n\nHmm, one subtle point: `checkQuantity` uses `Number.isInteger(qty)` — for example qty = 2.5 → not an integer → RangeError. qty = \"5\" → not an integer → RangeError. Good.\n\nR7: \"sorted by sku in plain code unit order (the `<` operator's ordering, not locale order)\". Fix to comparison function. Since skus are unique in a Map, a simple approach: `[...this.#items].sort(([a],[b]) => (a < b ? -1 : 1))` — but what about equal keys? There are no duplicate keys in a Map. But a full comparison is safer.\n\nAlso double-checking the R7 filter: \"SKUs with nothing on-hand and nothing reserved are excluded.\" The filter is `e.onHand > 0 || e.reserved > 0`. Good.\n\nWait — can onHand go negative? No, remove prevents onHand < reserved, and remove of an unknown sku is an error. Since add is the only increase, and remove requires onHand >= qty... actually remove requires qty <= onHand, so onHand stays >= 0. Good.\n\nAnother subtle point: in `remove`, when entry is undefined → RangeError. Per R6, remove on an unknown sku... the rule says \"otherwise remove throws a RangeError\" in the context of reserved stock. An unknown sku has reserved 0, and on-hand 0 < qty → RangeError. So treating undefined as RangeError is consistent.\n\nIn `release`, unknown sku → reserved 0 < qty → RangeError. Consistent.\n\nSo let's make the fixes:\n\n1. `release`: normalize the sku first (before or after checkQuantity — for \"does this first\", normalize first).\n2. `remove`: change the check from `qty > entry.onHand` to `qty > entry.onHand - entry.reserved` (on-hand can't drop below reserved).\n3. `snapshot`: sort in code unit order, not localeCompare.\n\nLet me write the edits and run the tests.\n","tool_calls":[{"id":"QkmhuwF1lzIf7N1mVcIVUxi9vJMH0IGs","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/tmp/endo-experiment-e1c38e4b487a/scratch/work/src/inventory.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"\\trelease(sku, qty) {\\n\\t\\tcheckQuantity(qty);\\n\\t\\tconst entry = this.#entry(sku);\",\"newText\":\"\\trelease(sku, qty) {\\n\\t\\tconst key = normalizeSku(sku);\\n\\t\\tcheckQuantity(qty);\\n\\t\\tconst entry = this.#entry(key);\"},{\"oldText\":\"\\t\\tif (entry === undefined || qty > entry.onHand) throw new RangeError(`cannot remove ${qty}`);\",\"newText\":\"\\t\\tif (entry === undefined || qty > entry.onHand - entry.reserved) throw new RangeError(`cannot remove ${qty}`);\"},{\"oldText\":\"\\t\\t\\t.sort((a, b) => a.sku.localeCompare(b.sku));\",\"newText\":\"\\t\\t\\t.sort((a, b) => (a.sku < b.sku ? -1 : a.sku > b.sku ? 1 : 0));\"}]}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"Successfully replaced 3 block(s) in /tmp/endo-experiment-e1c38e4b487a/scratch/work/src/inventory.js.","tool_call_id":"QkmhuwF1lzIf7N1mVcIVUxi9vJMH0IGs"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Now run the tests and verify edge cases against every rule:\n\n","reasoning_content":"Alright, let's run the tests and also verify a few additional edge cases against all the rules:\n","tool_calls":[{"id":"D1TF0Tt7ly0H4lguQ9toDIDyj5ASkFay","type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","arguments":"{\"command\":